WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:01.570
- Class A CDL drivers,

00:00:01.570 --> 00:00:04.380
we are hiring for regional
positions in your area,

00:00:04.380 --> 00:00:06.290
and we're giving away
the largest sign-on bonus

00:00:06.290 --> 00:00:10.390
that we've ever given,
$10,000, that's right, $10,000.

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.910
- [Narrator] This might seem extreme,

00:00:11.910 --> 00:00:14.300
but offers like these
are becoming more common

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.750
for truck driving jobs,

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.330
that's because amid a
global supply chain crunch

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.200
with mounting shipping delays,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.680
the US trucking industry needs drivers,

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:24.150
and it needs them now.

00:00:24.150 --> 00:00:26.900
- For truck drivers, demand is high.

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:30.100
People are desperate to get them,

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.590
because there's this big volume of stuff

00:00:32.590 --> 00:00:33.550
that needs to get moved,

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.680
and trucks move about
70%, maybe a bit more,

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:38.350
of the freight in the US.

00:00:38.350 --> 00:00:39.240
- [Narrator] Current estimates

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.350
from the American Trucking Associations

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:44.000
show there is a shortage
of 80,000 truck drivers

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.820
on the road, which is a
30% increase from 2019,

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:50.300
and a record high for the industry.

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.750
If the trend continues,
that number could grow

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.040
to 160,000 by 2028.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:59.450
- The market that we're
in today is requiring,

00:00:59.450 --> 00:01:02.160
and I think will continue to
require for a period of time,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:05.300
very strategic move is
relative to incentives,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:09.710
and to ways that we are
attracting and retaining drivers.

00:01:09.710 --> 00:01:11.410
- [Narrator] Knight-Swift Transportation,

00:01:11.410 --> 00:01:14.030
the largest truckload
carrier in North America,

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:15.980
is among the companies
that have boosted pay

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.640
to try to attract drivers.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:19.780
The company said it's
driving school graduates

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.010
are on track to earn
more than $60,000 a year

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:24.910
in their first year after training,

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:28.110
and as high as a 100,000 in some markets,

00:01:28.110 --> 00:01:29.700
that's more than double the median pay

00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:32.390
for truck drivers in
the US earned in 2020.

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:34.870
And industry-wide, the
average weekly earnings

00:01:34.870 --> 00:01:36.460
for long haul truckload drivers

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:40.730
are up more than 25% since
the beginning of 2019.

00:01:40.730 --> 00:01:43.270
- It's always a little bit of
a challenge hiring drivers,

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:45.730
particularly for these
long distance trucking jobs

00:01:45.730 --> 00:01:47.180
where people are away from home,

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:49.210
the conditions can be kind of grueling.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:50.960
- [Narrator] One incentive
some trucking companies

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:54.900
are offering to attract new
drivers, sign-on bonuses.

00:01:54.900 --> 00:01:58.050
84% of truck driver jobs
on employment marketplace,

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:01.740
ZipRecruiter, have included
some mention of bonus this year.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.990
- There's always a market effect

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:05.290
where if you need people,
you start to pay more,

00:02:05.290 --> 00:02:07.140
you offer bonuses, you do onboard,

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:08.800
you also have to get them trained up,

00:02:08.800 --> 00:02:10.080
and that can take some time

00:02:10.080 --> 00:02:11.460
if you're trying to recruit people

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:13.490
who weren't in the industry before.

00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.370
- [Narrator] One of the
biggest US trucking companies,

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.840
Yellow Corporation, said they have hosted

00:02:17.840 --> 00:02:20.900
at least 145 recruiting events this year,

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:23.220
and enrollment numbers
at each driver academies

00:02:23.220 --> 00:02:26.930
are up 500 percent compared with pre-pandemic numbers.

00:02:26.930 --> 00:02:28.850
Knight-Swift plans to more than double

00:02:28.850 --> 00:02:31.030
its number of company training locations

00:02:31.030 --> 00:02:33.300
to meet the increased demand for drivers.

00:02:33.300 --> 00:02:36.980
- I think it's fair to say that
there is more pressure today

00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:39.810
than we've seen in a
long time, perhaps ever,

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.750
even as we think through
the driver dynamic,

00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:46.860
the pandemic had impact
in the drivers sourcing.

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:48.690
- [Narrator] The trucking
industry's challenges

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.480
have come into focus recently

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:53.060
as a crush of imports overwhelms ports,

00:02:53.060 --> 00:02:56.220
and US retailers struggled
to restock inventories

00:02:56.220 --> 00:02:58.490
that emptied out during the pandemic,

00:02:58.490 --> 00:03:00.850
but the driver shortage is not new.

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.530
- Depending on who you've talked
to in the trucking sector,

00:03:03.530 --> 00:03:04.940
there's been a driver shortage

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:07.890
for something like two or three decades.

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:10.840
It does have a lot of churn,
there's a lot of turnover,

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.170
it's a tough job,

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.400
and it can pay fairly
well for blue collar work,

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.370
but you put in a lot of hours.

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:19.440
- [Narrator] The American
Trucking Associations

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:21.900
say there is a 90% annual turnover rate

00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:23.850
at large truckload carriers,

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:27.150
and the average age of drivers is 47.

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:29.010
According to the Labor Department,

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:32.690
women account for less than
8% of truck drivers in the US,

00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:35.230
and the industry skews
predominantly white.

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.120
- The trucking industry has
been concerned for a while,

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:39.810
they really wanna get younger
people in the pipeline,

00:03:39.810 --> 00:03:40.880
they wanna get more women,

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:42.430
they wanna try and get other people

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.360
excited about these driving jobs,

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.990
but it's been a little
bit of an uphill battle.

00:03:46.990 --> 00:03:48.350
- From a driver sourcing perspective,

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:49.840
we're seeing recovery in that,

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:51.880
relative to schools and training programs

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:54.823
and those kinds of things, but
there's just a gap to fill.

00:03:55.720 --> 00:03:57.220
- [Narrator] Even with
these new incentives,

00:03:57.220 --> 00:03:59.650
and an uptick in driver
training enrollment,

00:03:59.650 --> 00:04:01.430
there could still be a long road ahead

00:04:01.430 --> 00:04:03.670
to remedying the truck driver shortage

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:06.330
and unclogging the supply chain gridlock.

00:04:06.330 --> 00:04:07.280
- [Jennifer] The thing to remember

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.070
is that we are still in the
middle of a global pandemic,

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:13.070
so a lot of factors in the supply chain

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.820
rest on what's happening
in a factory overseas,

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:18.370
or how much capacity there is on a ship,

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:20.300
but you just sort of have
to take it as it comes,

00:04:20.300 --> 00:04:22.350
and hope that the different
kinks in the chain

00:04:22.350 --> 00:04:23.640
unkink themselves.

00:04:23.640 --> 00:04:26.223
(upbeat music)

